[b]v0.1.0:[/b]
[h1]Flavorium Universalis - Factions v0.1.0: First Release[/h1]

[i]Compatible with EU5 1.4.* | Requires: Flavorium Universalis[/i]

[hr][/hr]

[i]Early Alpha preview. Not yet played through; numbers will change.[/i]

First release. Political parties for every realm the mod simulates: four at a time out of eleven, chosen by government, age and estates, staffed by your ministers, and managed with political influence.

[list]
[*][b]Parties:[/b] Court, Aristocratic, Merchant, Clerical, War, Agrarian, Reform, Absolutist, Regional, Colonial and Liberal, with historical names in Holland, Italy, Sweden and Britain. Reviewed every fifteen to twenty-five years.
[*][b]Ministers:[/b] every minister belongs to a party, and works better or worse with its mood.
[*][b]Satisfaction and agendas:[/b] silent reviews every two to four years; agendas every five to twelve.
[*][b]Cabinet shape:[/b] stacked and balanced cabinets each have their own benefits and costs.
[*][b]The chamber:[/b] seats come from the realm's locations by rank and estate power, in a chamber of 20 to 84 seats. Ministers bring appointed seats, and each party has a leader.
[*][b]Actions:[/b] bribe, attack, ask a favour, appoint the leader or concede the agenda of the selected party, or call an election.
[*][b]Escalation:[/b] the War, Regional and Liberal parties escalate to a coup, a rising or an uprising if ignored.
[*][b]Liberal Thought:[/b] spreads through cities from the Age of Absolutism and brings the Liberal Party and term limits.
[/list]

With this submod loaded, Flavorium Universalis's estate-capture events, court-captured modifiers and balanced-court bonus give way to the party versions in realms that have parties.
